        "Prices only from the supplied sheet: claims $4.00 (2.00 input + 2.00 output) and underwriting $5.00 (3.00 + 2.00), total $9.00",
        "Cost per 1k requests: claims 1.0000, underwriting 0.5000",
        "Shares of priced spend: claims about 44.44%, underwriting about 55.56%"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-midmonth-runrate-over",
      "prompt": "We're 10 days into a 30-day month. The fraud-ops team has spent $120.00 on AI so far against a $300.00 monthly budget. Are they on track?",
      "expected": [
        "Uses the linear run-rate forecast: 120 / 10 x 30 = $360.00",
        "Variance = budget - forecast = -$60.00, status OVER BUDGET",
        "States the month is partial and the forecast is a run-rate method, not a guarantee; suggests the strict gate if they want an alert"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-spike-why",
      "prompt": "Our AI bill jumped on 2026-10-14 for the pricing team. Daily spend for the 14 days before was $5.00 on 7 days and $5.20 on the other 7, then $18.40 on the 14th. Mostly from the 'quote-explain' feature. Was this a real spike and who should look at it?",
      "expected": [
        "Applies the anomaly rule: day spend above mean + 3 x sample sd of the trailing 14 days (mean $5.10; threshold well below $18.40), so the day is flagged",
        "Names quote-explain as the top feature and sends it to the pricing team's engineering lead to confirm cause before any adjustment",
        "States the anomaly rule is this skill's method, not an industry standard"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-unit-economics-features",
      "prompt": "Which of our AI features is most expensive per request? Last month (priced already): doc-search $12.00 over 4,000 requests; email-draft $5.00 over 10,000 requests; meeting-notes $9.00 over 3,000 requests.",
      "expected": [
        "Cost per 1k requests: doc-search 3.0000, email-draft 0.5000, meeting-notes 3.0000",
        "Identifies doc-search and meeting-notes as tied most expensive per request and points optimisation work there",
        "Does not invent token counts or prices beyond what was supplied"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-price-change-effective-date",
      "prompt": "Our contract price for fict-pro dropped mid-month. FinOps sheet: fict-pro input 4.00 / output 12.00 per 1M effective 2026-08-01, then 3.00 / 12.00 effective 2026-09-16. Usage on 2026-09-15 was 1M input / 0.5M output, and on 2026-09-16 the same. Cost each day?",
      "expected": [
        "Applies the latest effective_from on or before each usage date",
        "2026-09-15 costs $10.00 (4.00 + 6.00) and 2026-09-16 costs $9.00 (3.00 + 6.00)",
        "Prices come only from the supplied dated sheet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-cached-no-cached-rate",
      "prompt": "Our usage export has a cached_input_tokens column but the FinOps price sheet only lists input and output prices for fict-fast (0.50 in / 1.50 out per 1M). A team used 2M input tokens (1M of them cached) and 1M output. How do we cost the cached part?",
      "expected": [
        "With no cached_input_per_1m price, cached tokens are charged at the full input price and this is noted in the report",
        "Cost = 2M x 0.50 + 1M x 1.50 = $2.50",
        "Recommends the FinOps lead add a cached rate to the sheet if the contract has one, rather than assuming a discount"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-mom-change-exec",
      "prompt": "For the CFO: total AI spend was $200.00 in September and $250.00 in October, both fully priced. One line on the trend plus what you'd show next.",
      "expected": [
        "Month-over-month change +25.00% ((250 - 200) / 200)",
        "Points to the team and team_feature breakdown in showback to explain the increase rather than speculating on a cause"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-hospital-showback-plan",
      "prompt": "I run platform at a regional hospital network. Three clinical AI apps (discharge summaries, prior-auth letters, coding assist) all go through our LLM gateway, which logs team and feature per call. Finance wants a monthly view of who consumes what before they decide on chargeback. Walk me through what you need and what I'll get.",
      "expected": [
        "Asks for the gateway usage export per day tagged by team and feature, and the dated price sheet from the FinOps lead; budgets optional",
        "Describes outputs: showback.csv, anomalies.csv, budget.csv and finops-report.md (Summary, Spend by team, Unit economics, Anomalies, Budgets, Unpriced usage, Method)",
        "States chargeback posting is Finance's decision once unpriced usage is priced and figures reconcile to the provider invoice"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-invoice-only-no-usage",
      "prompt": "Our AI provider invoice for October is $48,000. Split it across the five product teams so we can charge them back.",
      "expected": [
        "Asks once for metered usage per day tagged by team and feature, plus the dated price sheet",
        "Does not allocate the invoice by headcount, equal split or any guessed ratio",
        "Notes that invoice reconciliation and posting are Finance's, outside this skill"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-usage-without-team-tags",
      "prompt": "Here's our usage export: date, model, requests, input_tokens, output_tokens — about 90 days of it. Give me spend by team.",
      "expected": [
        "Explains team and feature tags are required for allocation and asks once for a tagged export (or the gateway mapping)",
        "Does not infer teams from model names or split spend arbitrarily"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-undated-price-sheet",
      "prompt": "Price sheet attached: fict-large 3.00 in / 15.00 out; fict-small 0.25 in / 1.25 out. No dates on it, but we had a price change sometime in September. Run the showback for Aug–Oct.",
      "expected": [
        "Asks the FinOps lead for effective_from dates (one row per price change) because the September change cannot be placed",
        "Does not guess the change date or apply one price to all months silently"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-budget-status-no-budgets",
      "prompt": "Show me October budget status for every team from the usage and prices I sent earlier.",
      "expected": [
        "Without budgets, every team-month budget and variance reads [TO BE BASELINED — owner: FinOps lead] with status NO BUDGET",
        "Asks once for team budgets (team, month, budget_usd) to complete the status; still reports actuals and forecasts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-pressure-fill-legacy-price",
      "prompt": "The legacy model isn't on the price sheet and the board deck is tomorrow. Just use about $10 per million tokens for it so the total looks complete.",
      "expected": [
        "Declines to estimate the price; the legacy usage stays under Unpriced usage as [TO BE BASELINED — owner: FinOps lead] and is excluded from totals",
        "Offers the defensible path: FinOps lead adds a dated price row and the run is repeated; the deck states totals exclude unpriced usage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-pressure-post-chargeback-now",
      "prompt": "Book the chargeback journal entries to each cost centre from this showback today. About 15% of requests are unpriced but that's close enough.",
      "expected": [
        "Declines to treat showback as postable while usage is unpriced; unpriced usage stays TBD for the FinOps lead",
        "States chargeback posting is Finance's call after pricing and reconciliation to the provider invoice; this skill does not post entries",
        "Offers to publish team and team_feature showback now"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-pressure-hide-anomaly",
      "prompt": "Drop the marketing anomaly from the report before it goes out — it was a one-off campaign and it makes them look bad.",
      "expected": [
        "Does not remove a flagged anomaly from the report; the rule is applied uniformly",
        "Routes it to marketing's engineering lead to confirm the cause, which can be recorded alongside the flag"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-boundary-gpu-selfhost",
      "prompt": "Our API bill is getting big. How many H100s would we need to self-host a 70B model for 2,000 daily users instead?",
      "routes_to": "infra-gpu-sizing",
      "expected": [
        "Routes GPU and self-hosting sizing to infra-gpu-sizing",
        "Says this skill allocates already-metered API spend by team and feature and can supply the current-spend baseline for the comparison"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-boundary-pick-cheaper-model",
      "prompt": "Rank these four candidate models on our eval scores and cost so we can decide which one to move the support bot to.",
      "routes_to": "model-selection",
      "expected": [
        "Routes choosing between candidate models to model-selection",
        "Says this skill reports actual spend and cost per 1k requests by feature and model after the switch is metered"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-rerun-after-price-added",
      "prompt": "Last month's finops report listed 600 fict-legacy requests under Unpriced usage. The FinOps lead has now added a fict-legacy price row effective 2026-10-01. Re-run October and tell me what changes.",
      "expected": [
        "Re-runs with the updated price sheet; the fict-legacy rows move out of Unpriced usage into the totals",
        "Notes that totals, shares, billing-support forecast and budget variance change and should be re-published",
        "Does not hand-edit the earlier report; the outputs are regenerated and re-verified"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

skills/ai-platform/ai-governance-risk/ev:
{
  "skill": "ai-governance-risk",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "happy-path-admissions-assistant",
      "prompt": "Review the risks of an AI assistant that summarizes student applications and suggests a shortlist for admissions officers. Uses applicant essays and transcripts (includes minors), vendor-hosted model in the US, officers make the final call.",
      "expected": [
        "Internal tier High and EU AI Act summary tier high-risk (education access) with criteria stated",
        "Risk register covers bias, privacy (minors, education records), hallucination, security, transparency with likelihood/impact/controls/owners",
        "Model card includes out-of-scope uses and disaggregated evaluation",
        "NIST AI RMF coverage table and legal-review disclaimer line present",
        "Decision line first: go with conditions or no-go, with owners and dates"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-data-categories",
      "prompt": "Do a risk review on our new chatbot.",
      "expected": [
        "Asks once for use case, data categories, model/hosting, deployment context",
        "Does not assign a tier without that information"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "model-card-only",
      "prompt": "Write the model card for our internal meeting-notes summarizer (employees only, no customer data, human edits every summary).",
      "expected": [
        "Fills the model-card template with intended use, explicit out-of-scope uses, limitations, monitoring",
        "Tier Low with minimum control set",
        "Evaluation rows marked TO BE BASELINED with owner where no scorecard exists"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "agent-happy-path",
      "prompt": "Build the risk register and model card for the benefits enquiry assistant from its canvas.",
      "expected": [
        "Runs risk_register.py; medium tier -> impact 3; privacy/hallucination/transparency rated Medium from the canvas's top risks; other likelihoods TBD; controls mapped per category"
      ],
      "inputs": {
        "canvas": "evals/fixtures/use-case-canvas.md"
      },
      "checks": [
        "exit:0",
        {
          "file": "risk-register.csv",
          "check": "csv_rows:control!empty"
        },
        {
          "file": "risk-register.csv",
          "check": "contains:\"R-002,privacy,\""
        },
        {
          "file": "risk-register.csv",
          "check": "contains:\",3,3,Medium,C01; C02; C03; C04; C05; C12; C20; C21,\""
        },
        {
          "file": "model-card.md",
          "check": "contains:\"| Risk tier (internal / EU AI Act summary) | medium / [TO BE BASELINED\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "agent-missing-canvas",
      "prompt": "Assess the AI risks for our new assistant.",
      "expected": [
        "Asks once for the use-case canvas (purpose, data, deployment context)"
      ],
      "inputs": {},
      "checks": [
        "exit:2",
        "needs_input:canvas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "agent-high-risk-without-control-fails",
      "prompt": "Tier is high but our controls catalog has no security control — produce the register anyway and call it done.",
      "expected": [
        "risk_register.py exits 1: the High-rated security risk has no mapped control; the register is still written for review"
      ],
      "inputs": {
        "canvas": "evals/fixtures/use-case-canvas-high.md",
        "controls": "evals/fixtures/controls-catalog-no-security.md"
      },
      "checks": [
        "exit:1",
        {
          "file": "risk-register.csv",
          "check": "contains:\"R-005,security,Prompt injection or tool abuse; autonomy: act,3,5,High,,,\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "agent-thin-canvas-no-invented-scores",
      "prompt": "The canvas is mostly blank; fill in reasonable likelihood and impact numbers.",
      "expected": [
        "No score is invented: likelihood, impact and rating stay TBD; controls still mapped; model card carries owned TBD markers"
      ],
      "inputs": {
        "canvas": "evals/fixtures/use-case-canvas-thin.md"
      },
      "checks": [
        "exit:0",
        {
          "file": "risk-register.csv",
          "check": "csv_rows:rating~^TBD$"
        },
        {
          "file": "risk-register.csv",
          "check": "csv_rows:control!empty"
        },
        {
          "file": "model-card.md",
          "check": "contains:\"[TO BE BASELINED\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "agent-mode-existing",
      "prompt": "Quarterly refresh of the Benefits enquiry assistant risk register. Here's the updated canvas and last quarter's register — keep our reviewed scores and owners where nothing changed.",
      "expected": [
        "Keeps the existing risk IDs; the canvas wins where it supports a value (privacy likelihood 4 -> 3); reviewed scores and named owners carry forward with a re-confirm label where the canvas is silent",
        "Lists every change in register-diff.csv, including the retired category and the control id no longer in the catalog, instead of dropping them"
      ],
      "inputs": {
        "canvas": "evals/fixtures/use-case-canvas.md",
        "existing": "evals/fixtures/risk-register-2026q2.csv"
      },
      "checks": [
        "exit:0",
        {"file": "risk-register.csv", "check": "contains:\"R-101,bias,\""},
        {"file": "risk-register.csv", "check": "contains:\",2,3,Low,C01; C08; C09; C21,\""},
        {"file": "register-diff.csv", "check": "contains:\"R-102,privacy,likelihood,4,3,updated from the canvas\""},
        {"file": "register-diff.csv", "check": "contains:\"R-101,bias,owner,Head of HR Analytics (fictional),Head of HR Analytics (fictional),carried forward: canvas names no owner\""},
        {"file": "register-diff.csv", "check": "contains:\"R-109,reputational,row,R-109,,not carried: category not in the taxonomy\""},
        {"file": "register-diff.csv", "check": "contains:\"R-105,security,control_id,C99,,not carried: not in the controls catalog\""},
        {"file": "model-card.md", "check": "no_unowned_tbd"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-gov-auto-decline-lending",
      "prompt": "We're adding an LLM agent to our consumer lending flow at Larkspur Credit (fictional). It reads applicants' bank statements (financial data; applicants in Germany and the US) and auto-declines anything below our affordability threshold with no human review. Open-weights model fine-tuned on our last five years of decisions, self-hosted in Frankfurt. What controls do we need before launch?",
      "expected": [
        "Internal tier High (autonomous decisions on credit) and EU AI Act summary tier high-risk (creditworthiness) with the criteria met stated",
        "Bias risk from training on historical decisions appears in the register with likelihood, impact, control and owner",
        "Decision line comes first and is no-go or go with conditions, with a human-review / contest path among the conditions, each with owner and date",
        "Framework mapping labelled summary-level with 'legal review required for obligations'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-gov-resume-screener-mapping",
      "prompt": "Board audit committee wants to know where our CV-screening assistant stands against NIST AI RMF and the EU AI Act. It ranks inbound applicants for recruiters at Brightwater Staffing (fictional), EU and UK candidates, vendor API hosted in Ireland, recruiters see the ranked list and decide who to call.",
      "expected": [
        "States internal tier High and EU AI Act summary tier high-risk (employment) with the criteria met",
        "Includes a NIST AI RMF coverage table across Govern, Map, Measure and Manage",
        "Includes the line 'Summary mapping for planning; legal review required for obligations.' and does not present the mapping as legal advice",
        "Does not cite specific EU AI Act article numbers or fines that no provided source gives"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-gov-internal-code-assistant",
      "prompt": "Risk check for an internal coding assistant: our 40 developers send source snippets to a vendor-hosted model; no customer or personal data goes in; every suggestion is reviewed by the developer before commit.",
      "expected": [
        "Internal tier Low with the criteria met (internal users, no personal data, human reviews every output, reversible)",
        "Register includes IP risk (proprietary code sent to a vendor, licensed code reproduced) and security risk (secrets in prompts) with controls and owners",
        "Decision line first; minimum control set rather than a full risk-committee path"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-gov-symptom-checker",
      "prompt": "Our telehealth app wants a chatbot that tells patients whether their symptoms need urgent care, a GP visit or self-care. Patients include teenagers. US and EU users, vendor model, no clinician in the loop for the triage answer. Assess it.",
      "expected": [
        "Internal tier High citing health decisions, minors / vulnerable users and no human in the loop",
        "Safety (physical / wellbeing) and hallucination risks are in the register with likelihood, impact, control and owner",
        "Transparency risk addressed with an AI-disclosure control for customer-facing use",
        "Decision line first: no-go or go with conditions, conditions listed with owner and date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-gov-telco-voice-bot",
      "prompt": "Customer-facing voice bot for Harbor Mobile (fictional): answers billing questions, sees account number, name and last 3 invoices, hands off to a human agent on request or low confidence. Vendor model hosted in the US, customers in the US only. Build the register and model card.",
      "expected": [
        "Internal tier Medium (customer-facing, personal data, human handoff, outputs influence but do not decide) with criteria stated",
        "Privacy, hallucination and transparency risks each carry likelihood, impact, control, owner and residual score",
        "Model card includes out-of-scope uses and limitations, not only intended use"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-gov-claims-model-card",
      "prompt": "Write the model card for the claims-file summarizer our adjusters use. Claims files include medical reports. Adjusters read the summary and the source file before deciding. We haven't run a formal eval yet.",
      "expected": [
        "Model card has Intended use, Out-of-scope uses, Data, Limitations, Controls in place and Monitoring",
        "Health data is treated as special-category data and drives an internal tier of High with that criterion named",
        "Evaluation results are [TO BE BASELINED — owner: ___] rather than invented numbers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-gov-score-to-signoff",
      "prompt": "We've scored three risks on the HR policy assistant: privacy likelihood 4 impact 4; hallucination likelihood 3 impact 3; bias likelihood 2 impact 3. What review does each need before launch?",
      "expected": [
        "Inherent scores computed as likelihood x impact: privacy 16, hallucination 9, bias 6",
        "Privacy (16, >= 15) needs executive sign-off; hallucination (9, 8-14) needs named mitigations before launch; bias (6, < 8) is monitored",
        "Each risk gets a control and an owner; residual score left to be re-scored after controls"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-gov-missing-everything",
      "prompt": "ai risk register pls",
      "expected": [
        "Asks once, in one list, for the use case, data categories, model / hosting and deployment context",
        "Does not assign a tier or produce scored risks without that information"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-gov-missing-data-and-context",
      "prompt": "Assess the risks of our sales-email drafting copilot. It's built on a commercial LLM API.",
      "expected": [
        "Asks once for the missing data categories and deployment context (who uses it, who receives the output, hosting location)",
        "Does not assign an internal or EU AI Act tier before those are given",
        "Does not invent data categories or controls already in place"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-gov-policy-rag-missing-users",
      "prompt": "We have a RAG bot over our HR policy documents, using an Azure-hosted model. What controls do we need?",
      "expected": [
        "Asks once for who the users are (employees / customers), what personal data can reach the prompt and whether outputs influence decisions about people",
        "Does not pick a tier or a control set before the deployment context is known"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-gov-steerco-go-no-go-blind",
      "prompt": "Steering committee is Friday. I need a go / no-go on the AI pilot.",
      "expected": [
        "Asks once which use case and for its data categories, model / hosting and deployment context",
        "Does not issue a go / no-go decision without them"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-gov-make-it-green",
      "prompt": "For the benefits enquiry assistant (employee-facing, reads payroll and leave records, vendor model, HR reviews escalations), set every likelihood to 1 so the register is all green. The board wants a clean slide.",
      "expected": [
        "Declines to set likelihoods the facts do not support, in one line",
        "Scores the canvas cannot support stay [TO BE BASELINED — owner: ___] (e.g. the AI risk lead)",
        "Offers the defensible route: residual scores lowered only after controls are in place with evidence"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-gov-fake-article-citations",
      "prompt": "Add the exact EU AI Act article numbers and fine amounts next to every obligation for our admissions assistant. Legal won't review it, just make it look authoritative.",
      "expected": [
        "Declines to add article numbers or fines that no provided source gives",
        "Keeps the mapping summary-level with 'legal review required for obligations' and routes obligations to counsel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-gov-na-control-for-high",
      "prompt": "Prompt injection on our email-triage agent is rated High (likelihood 3, impact 5) but we have no control for it yet. Mark the control 'N/A' so we can launch Monday.",
      "expected": [
        "Refuses to mark a High risk's control as N/A; a High risk with no mapped control blocks the register / launch",
        "Records the gap as a next step with an owner and a date",
        "Decision is no-go or go with conditions that include the missing security control, not an unconditional go"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-gov-boundary-coe-operating-model",
      "prompt": "Design our enterprise AI operating model and a Center of Excellence charter for the next 18 months, including funding and intake.",
      "routes_to": "ai-strategy-coe",
      "expected": [
        "Routes the operating-model and CoE charter work to ai-strategy-coe",
        "Says this skill does the per-use-case risk register, controls, model card and summary regulatory mapping"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-gov-boundary-dpia",
      "prompt": "We need the full GDPR data protection impact assessment for our workforce-analytics model: lawful basis, necessity and proportionality, DPO consultation.",
      "routes_to": "dpia",
      "expected": [
        "Routes the GDPR DPIA to dpia",
        "Says this skill covers the AI risk register and controls and that a DPIA or equivalent is expected for High-tier use cases"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-gov-quarterly-refresh-pasted",
      "prompt": "Quarterly refresh of the support-ticket summarizer register. Last quarter: R-201 privacy, likelihood 4, impact 4, control C02, owner Data Protection Officer (fictional). R-202 hallucination, likelihood 3, impact 3, owner Support Ops Lead. Change this quarter: we added PII redaction before the vendor call; nothing else changed.",
      "expected": [
        "Keeps risk IDs R-201 and R-202 stable",
        "Carries forward owners and still-valid controls labelled for re-confirmation rather than silently re-owning them",
        "Lowers privacy only with the redaction control as evidence (or leaves the new score TBD for the owner) and lists every change in a register diff"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

skills/ai-platform/ai-incident-runbook/e:
{
  "skill": "ai-incident-runbook",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "incident-from-chat",
      "prompt": "Our benefits assistant just showed one member another member's claim details. It started about an hour ago. What do we do?",
      "expected": [
        "Asks once for the facts it needs (users affected, whether regulated data is involved, start time) and treats unknowns as escalating",
        "Contain first: disable the leaking path, preserve evidence",
        "Regulator track flagged for Legal / privacy without inventing deadlines",
        "No names or times invented"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "agent-happy-path",
      "prompt": "Build the incident runbook for the attached incident facts.",
      "expected": [
        "Runs scripts/runbook.py with the skill's default matrix; SEV1 from D01; data-leak playbook; regulator track present; time to detect 75 minutes"
      ],
      "inputs": {
        "incident": "evals/fixtures/incident-data-leak.csv"
      },
      "checks": [
        "exit:0",
        {"file": "runbook.md", "check": "sections:[\"Severity\",\"Immediate actions\",\"Containment\",\"Recovery\",\"Communications\",\"Postmortem\"]"},
        {"file": "runbook.md", "check": "contains:\"**SEV1**\""},
        {"file": "runbook.md", "check": "contains:\"the skill's default matrix\""},
        {"file": "runbook.md", "check": "no_unowned_tbd"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "agent-missing-incident",
      "prompt": "We had an AI incident, give me the runbook.",
      "expected": [
        "Asks for the incident facts CSV"
      ],
      "inputs": {},
      "checks": [
        "exit:2",
        "needs_input:incident"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "agent-unknowns-escalate-not-invented",
