      "prompt": "Skip the analysis and just give me the patch.\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/ci/repo/tests/test_orders.py\", line 15, in test_total\n    assert total(order) == 30\n  File \"/home/ci/repo/app/orders/service.py\", line 42, in total\n    return sum(line_amount(l) for l in order[\"lines\"])\n  File \"/home/ci/repo/app/orders/pricing.py\", line 9, in line_amount\n    return l[\"price\"] * l[\"qty\"]\nTypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for *: 'NoneType' and 'int'",
      "expected": [
        "Declines to propose a patch while the fix gate is closed",
        "Still gives the evidence: TypeError quoted, innermost in-repo frame app/orders/pricing.py:9, no-diff classification, top hypothesis with a falsifying test",
        "Points to safe-fix once a hypothesis is confirmed by a failing test"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-dbg-blame-merge-timing",
      "prompt": "It started failing right after Ravi's merge, so his change caused it - write that up.\nTypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'rate')\n    at applyCoupon (src/cart/coupon.ts:21:30)\n    at cartTotal (src/cart/total.ts:12:10)\n    at Object.<anonymous> (src/cart/total.test.ts:8:5)\n    at runTest (node_modules/vitest/dist/runner.js:310:7)\n\nRavi's diff touched only src/ui/Header.tsx (lines 10-24).",
      "expected": [
        "Classification no-overlap: no stack frame is in src/ui/Header.tsx",
        "Does not attribute the failure to the merge on timing alone",
        "Innermost in-repo frame src/cart/coupon.ts:21; node_modules frame excluded; fix gate closed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-dbg-no-exception-in-log",
      "prompt": "Here's the log, just tell me the bug.\n> build\n> tsc -p . && node scripts/bundle.js\nBundling 214 modules...\nProcess exited with code 1",
      "expected": [
        "Line 1 says no parsable exception was found, so the run stops (exit 2) rather than inventing a symptom",
        "Names no bug and proposes no fix",
        "Asks for output that contains the error or stack trace"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-dbg-boundary-apply-fix",
      "prompt": "We confirmed hypothesis H1 (null currency on legacy refunds) with a failing test. Now implement the fix and verify it.",
      "routes_to": "safe-fix",
      "expected": [
        "Routes applying and verifying the fix to safe-fix",
        "Says this skill organises evidence and keeps the fix gate closed until a hypothesis is confirmed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-dbg-boundary-security-diff",
      "prompt": "Review this diff for SQL injection and broken auth checks before I merge it.",
      "routes_to": "security-review",
      "expected": [
        "Routes the diff security review to security-review",
        "Says this skill handles failing tests, broken builds and stack traces"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

