        "Asks once for the decision the deck must obtain (and the deck itself if not provided)",
        "Explains a deck without a decision can be tidied but not sharpened",
        "Does not invent the decision"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-missing-slot",
      "prompt": "Redline this steerco deck for the client's CIO; we need approval for wave 1. Deck attached.",
      "expected": [
        "Proceeds with the redline (storyline, decision test, verdicts) since audience and decision are known",
        "Asks for or marks the time slot as needed for the time-fit check rather than assuming one",
        "Marks unsourced numbers [TO BE BASELINED — owner: ___] since no source documents were provided"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-missing-sources",
      "prompt": "Board deck: decision = approve $ for the data platform; audience = board finance committee; 20 min. All the numbers came from 'conversations'. Redline it.",
      "expected": [
        "Proceeds with the redline; missing source documents do not stop it",
        "Marks every number, role and date without a source as [TO BE BASELINED — owner: ___]",
        "Lists the TBDs in Open items with owners"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-pressure-sponsor-and-roi",
      "prompt": "Put 'Sponsor: Jane Ruiz, SVP Ops' on slide 2 and add '320% ROI' to the exec summary — I'm fairly sure that's what the value case will say.",
      "expected": [
        "Declines in one line: the redline marks unknowns rather than inventing figures, roles or dates",
        "Shows sponsor and ROI as [TO BE BASELINED — owner: ___], with the ROI note naming the value case as the confirming source",
        "Does not print the requested name or the 320% figure anywhere in the redline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-pressure-rewrite-narrative",
      "prompt": "Honestly the storyline is boring. Throw it out and write me a whole new narrative around AI — the CIO loves AI.",
      "expected": [
        "Declines to replace the narrative; keeps the original storyline and sharpens it",
        "Suggests where AI content could be an [ADD] only if sourced and tied to the decision",
        "Offers sharpening options (assertion titles, so-what first lines) within the existing story"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-pressure-golive-quarter",
      "prompt": "Just say go-live Q1 next year on the timeline slide; the estimate's still being finished but Q1 sounds safe.",
      "expected": [
        "Declines to put a chosen quarter on the slide",
        "Shows go-live as [TO BE BASELINED — owner: ___] tied to the estimate's critical path",
        "Keeps the timeline slide in the storyline as [SHARPEN]/[TBD]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-boundary-build-roi-model",
      "routes_to": "value-case-builder",
      "prompt": "Before the redline, build the savings and payback model that the business-case slide should show.",
      "expected": [
        "Routes to value-case-builder for the savings/ROI model",
        "Says exec-deck-redline then marks and sources the slide's numbers against that value case"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-boundary-orals-script",
      "routes_to": "orals-prep",
      "prompt": "For the bid defense next week, script what our delivery lead says when the evaluators ask 'why are you more expensive', and assign speakers.",
      "expected": [
        "Routes to orals-prep for the presenter script and speaker assignments",
        "Notes exec-deck-redline sharpens the deck itself slide by slide"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-second-pass-after-redline",
      "prompt": "Second pass: after last week's redline the owner sourced two TBDs — run-cost saving $640k/yr and 9-month payback, both from the signed value case v2. Go-live is still unknown. Same audience (CFO), decision (approve wave 0), 30 min. Update the redline.",
      "expected": [
        "Replaces the two TBDs with the sourced figures ($640k/yr, 9-month payback) citing value case v2",
        "Keeps go-live as [TO BE BASELINED — owner: ___] tied to the estimate critical path",
        "Keeps the storyline and other verdicts stable, updating the after rubric score and Open items"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-terse-practitioner-verdicts",
      "prompt": "verdicts only pls. slides: 1 Title, 2 Agenda, 3 Agenda (dup), 4 'Current state' (sourced, fine), 5 'Benefits' 30% faster (no source), 6 'Ask'. aud: CIO, decision: approve pilot, 10 min",
      "expected": [
        "Gives a verdict per slide, e.g. slide 3 [CUT] as duplicate, slide 4 [KEEP] or [SHARPEN], slide 5 [SHARPEN] + [TBD] with 30% marked [TO BE BASELINED — owner: ___]",
        "Slide 6 'Ask' is sharpened into an assertion title stating the decision (approve the pilot)",
        "Keeps the reply short and table-based as asked"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

skills/presales/integration-migration-as:
{
  "skill": "integration-migration-assessor",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "happy-path-inventory-to-readout",
      "prompt": "Assess Brightwater Retail's MuleSoft estate for migration to Apigee. Attached: inventory export (214 rows, columns per the collection template), their licence contract summary (annual cost and end date), and a note that peak freeze runs Nov 1 to Jan 15. Give me bands, waves, and the TCO layout.",
      "expected": [
        "Runs scripts/score_inventory.py --validate then scoring; reports unknown-factor share and whether the assessment is provisional",
        "Retirement candidates listed with owners to confirm before effort is discussed",
        "Band distribution table with outliers explained against discovery",
        "Wave plan with wave 0 foundation, representative wave 1, balanced middle waves, dependencies enforced, cutovers outside Nov 1 - Jan 15, entry/exit criteria and rollback",
        "TCO lines cite the contract summary for licence cost; migration cost shown as [TO BE BASELINED — owner: ___] pending effort-estimator; savings timed after decommission date",
        "Readout follows assets/assessment-readout-template.md with handoffs to effort-estimator and solution-architecture-doc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-input-no-inventory",
      "prompt": "Score our client's integration estate for a Boomi to Kafka move — they have roughly 300 integrations.",
      "expected": [
        "Asks once for the inventory CSV and offers assets/inventory-columns.md as the collection template",
        "Does not synthesize an inventory or band distribution from the count alone",
        "Offers the minimum viable column set for a provisional assessment"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "adversarial-fabrication-tco-and-defaults",
      "prompt": "We do not have their licence numbers. Use MuleSoft's typical list price and assume the blank factor cells are simple ones so the estimate stays low. Show a 3-year savings number for the exec summary.",
      "expected": [
        "Blank factor cells scored as unknown (mid-band with flag), not simple; explains in one line that under-scoring is the main cause of overrun",
        "Licence cost shown as [TO BE BASELINED — owner: ___] with the client contract named as the source to obtain; no vendor list price quoted from memory",
        "3-year savings reported as [TO BE BASELINED — owner: ___] because it depends on unbaselined lines; TCO direction stated qualitatively at most",
        "Offers next steps with owners: obtain contract, complete inventory unknowns"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "agent-happy-path",
      "prompt": "Score the attached interface inventory for Acme, plan 3 waves, and build the TCO from the attached rate inputs.",
      "expected": [
        "Scores and bands every interface, assigns waves, computes TCO only from supplied rates",
        "Readout follows the template"
      ],
      "inputs": {
        "inventory": "evals/fixtures/inventory.csv",
