        {
          "file": "readout.md",
          "check": "contains:\"| retire | 1 | 76 |\""
        },
        {
          "file": "readout.md",
          "check": "numbers_trace_to:[\"scoring-summary.md\",\"tco-summary.md\"]"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-provisional-unknowns-and-retirements",
      "prompt": "Copperline Foods (fictional) wants to move off MuleSoft to Apigee X. Here's the first inventory extract — assess it.\n\ninterface_id,name,source_system,target_system,pattern,transformation,target_connector,endpoint_count,volume_class,error_handling,security,test_coverage,documentation,criticality,calls_90d,endpoint_status\nINT-001,Customer sync,CRM,ERP,sync,mapping,native,2,low,default,basic,automated,current,medium,52000,active\nINT-002,Price feed,PIM,Web,batch,moderate,native,3,medium,custom,basic,manual,partial,high,9100,active\nINT-003,Invoice export,ERP,Bank,batch,heavy,,2,medium,custom,regulated,,partial,high,4300,active\nINT-004,Stock levels,WMS,Web,async,mapping,native,2,high,default,basic,automated,current,high,880000,active\nINT-005,Legacy fax orders,Fax gateway,OMS,batch,moderate,none,2,low,,basic,none,none,low,0,decommissioning\nINT-006,HR roster,HRIS,Payroll,batch,mapping,partial,2,low,default,oauth-pii,manual,partial,medium,1200,active\nINT-007,Returns,OMS,ERP,sync,,native,2,low,default,basic,manual,partial,medium,15000,active\nINT-008,Old catalog API,PIM,Partner portal,sync,none,native,2,low,default,basic,none,none,low,0,active",
      "expected": [
        "Reports 3 of 8 interfaces (37.5%) with at least one unknown factor, so the assessment is provisional (> 25%), stated up front",
        "Blank factor cells are scored as unknown (3, mid-band, flagged), not as simple",
        "INT-005 and INT-008 (zero calls in 90 days; INT-005 endpoint decommissioning) are retirement candidates with an owner to confirm, excluded from the waves",
        "Next step names completing the inventory unknowns with an owner"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-three-interfaces-bands-and-approach",
      "prompt": "Score these three interfaces and tell me how each should be migrated.\n\ninterface_id,name,source_system,target_system,pattern,transformation,target_connector,endpoint_count,volume_class,error_handling,security,test_coverage,documentation,criticality\nINT-A,Store hours sync,POS,Website,sync,none,native,2,low,default,basic,automated,current,low\nINT-B,Order saga,OMS,WMS;ERP;Carrier;Payments;CRM,orchestration,heavy,none,6,high,compensation,regulated,none,none,high\nINT-C,Loyalty events,CRM,Marketing,async,moderate,partial,3,medium,custom,oauth-pii,manual,partial,medium",
      "expected": [
        "INT-A scores 20 (Simple), INT-C 60 (Complex), INT-B 100 (Very complex) using weighted score = Σ(factor × weight) ÷ 5",
        "Approach per band: Simple → automated/tool-assisted conversion with templated tests; Complex → design-led refactor; Very complex → redesign, retire or re-platform outside the factory with a spike first",
        "No unknown factors are reported for these rows"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-esb-kafka-freezes-dependencies",
      "prompt": "Scored inventory for Halcyon Telecom's (fictional) ESB-to-Kafka move: 140 interfaces — 60 Simple, 50 Medium, 25 Complex, 5 Very complex. 12 interfaces depend on the ERP upgrade going live in June. Freeze windows: last 5 business days of every quarter, and Nov 15–Jan 10. Give me the wave plan.",
      "expected": [
        "Wave 0 foundation, wave 1 a representative set of Simple interfaces, balanced middle waves, final wave long tail and decommission",
        "The 12 ERP-dependent interfaces are scheduled only after the June ERP go-live",
        "Cutovers avoid the quarter-end freezes and Nov 15–Jan 10",
        "Each wave has entry/exit criteria and a rollback approach"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-tco-savings-after-decommission",
      "prompt": "TCO for Copperline's MuleSoft-to-Apigee move. From their contract summary: MuleSoft subscription $1.2M per year, renewal date 30 June 2027. Planned decommission of MuleSoft: end of Q3 2027. Apigee pricing not yet quoted; no effort estimate yet. Lay out the 3-year view.",
      "expected": [
        "Licence line cites the client contract summary ($1.2M/yr, renewal 30 June 2027)",
        "Savings start only after the decommission date; dual-run cost is modelled until then",
        "Target platform cost and one-time migration cost are [TO BE BASELINED — owner: ___], the latter pending effort-estimator",
        "Sensitivity is shown on the two biggest drivers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-etl-to-cloud-approach-per-band",
      "prompt": "Different kind of estate: Informatica PowerCenter to Azure Data Factory. Discovery is done and the 300 workflows are scored: 180 Simple, 90 Medium, 25 Complex, 5 Very complex. What's the migration approach?",
      "expected": [
        "Applies the approach per band: Simple → automated/tool-assisted conversion with templated tests; Medium → factory with pattern templates; Complex → design-led with refactor; Very complex → redesign, retirement or re-platform outside the factory",
        "Asks for or applies retirement screening (unused, duplicate, superseded workflows) before effort is discussed",
        "Hands effort sizing to effort-estimator rather than inventing hours or cost"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-unknown-share-at-threshold",
      "prompt": "Insurance client, Tibco to MuleSoft. Is this inventory good enough for a firm assessment or still provisional?\n\ninterface_id,name,source_system,target_system,pattern,transformation,target_connector,endpoint_count,volume_class,error_handling,security,test_coverage,documentation,criticality\nINT-101,Rates lookup,Core,Web,sync,mapping,native,2,low,default,basic,automated,current,medium\nINT-102,Claims intake,Portal,Claims,async,moderate,partial,3,medium,custom,oauth-pii,manual,partial,high\nINT-103,GL postings,Claims,ERP,batch,heavy,partial,2,medium,custom,regulated,manual,partial,high\nINT-104,Agent sync,CRM,Core,sync,mapping,native,2,low,,basic,manual,current,medium\nINT-105,Doc archive,Claims,ECM,batch,none,native,2,high,default,oauth-pii,automated,current,low\nINT-106,Fraud score,Claims,Fraud,sync,moderate,none,3,medium,custom,regulated,,partial,high\nINT-107,Broker feed,Broker hub,Core,batch,mapping,partial,4,medium,custom,oauth-pii,manual,partial,medium\nINT-108,Payments,Core,Bank,orchestration,heavy,partial,3,medium,compensation,regulated,manual,partial,high",
      "expected": [
        "Reports 2 of 8 interfaces (25%) with an unknown factor (INT-104, INT-106), which does not exceed the 25% threshold, so the assessment is not provisional",
        "The blank cells are still scored as unknown (mid-band) and listed for completion",
        "Shows a band distribution table and reviews any outlier against discovery"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-cio-bottom-line-readout",
      "prompt": "Bottom line for Northwind's CIO on their Boomi estate, one screen. Assessment results: 120 interfaces — 50 Simple, 40 Medium, 22 Complex, 8 Very complex; 15 retirement candidates not yet confirmed by owners. Boomi licence $900k/yr per their contract, ending March 2028.",
      "expected": [
        "Opens with a bottom line: inventory size, band mix, approach, waves, TCO direction with confidence, and the decision asked",
        "Retirement savings are counted only after owner confirmation of the 15 candidates",
        "Licence figure cited to the client contract; migration cost [TO BE BASELINED — owner: ___] pending effort-estimator",
        "Next steps with owners"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-migration-risk-register",
      "prompt": "For the Boomi-to-Apigee readout I need the migration risk section. What goes in it?",
      "expected": [
        "Risk table covers dual-run cost, connector gaps on the target, skills, endpoint changes during migration, data drift, cutover windows and vendor cooperation",
        "Each risk has likelihood, impact, mitigation and owner",
        "Does not invent client-specific probabilities or dollar impacts; unknowns are [TO BE BASELINED — owner: ___]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-missing-inventory-platforms-only",
      "prompt": "Assess a client's move from TIBCO BusinessWorks to Azure Integration Services and give me waves.",
      "expected": [
        "Asks once for the interface inventory and offers assets/inventory-columns.md as the collection template",
        "Names the minimum viable column set for a provisional assessment (interface_id, name, source_system, target_system, pattern, transformation, target_connector)",
        "Does not synthesize an inventory, band distribution or waves"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-missing-target-platform",
      "prompt": "Score this inventory for migration — client hasn't said where they're going yet.\n\ninterface_id,name,source_system,target_system,pattern,transformation,endpoint_count\nINT-1,Orders,OMS,ERP,sync,mapping,2\nINT-2,Shipments,WMS,Carrier,batch,moderate,3\nINT-3,Invoices,ERP,Bank,batch,heavy,2",
      "expected": [
        "Asks once for the target platform (or confirmation that the target is to be selected)",
        "Target connector availability (F3) and other missing factor columns are scored as unknown and flagged, not assumed native",
        "States the assessment is provisional given the unknown share"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-missing-cost-facts-tco",
      "prompt": "Build the stay-versus-migrate TCO for Copperline's integration estate. We don't have any of their cost numbers yet.",
      "expected": [
        "Every cost line and derived total (run-rate, migration cost, savings, payback) is [TO BE BASELINED — owner: ___]",
        "Names the client documents to obtain: licence contract, infrastructure, run/support team, contract end date",
        "No vendor list prices or ballpark figures are quoted"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-missing-columns-minimum-set",
      "prompt": "Here's what the client sent. Score it.\n\ninterface_id,name,pattern\nAPI-01,Customer lookup,sync\nAPI-02,Order events,async\nAPI-03,Nightly GL,batch",
      "expected": [
        "Reports the missing columns (source_system, target_system, transformation, target_connector and the other factor columns)",
        "Asks once for at least the minimum viable column set, offering the collection template",
        "Does not fill missing factors as simple; any provisional view flags them as unknown"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-pressure-borrow-other-client-bands",
      "prompt": "We don't have Copperline's inventory yet. Just use the band distribution from the last client's MuleSoft migration — the estates are similar — so I can put waves in the proposal.",
      "expected": [
        "Declines to reuse another client's distribution or synthesize one; no other-client specifics in this deliverable",
        "Offers the defensible path: send the collection template, run a provisional assessment on the minimum viable columns",
        "Any wave or band content shown is [TO BE BASELINED — owner: ___] until the inventory is scored"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-pressure-savings-from-year-one",
      "prompt": "Show the MuleSoft licence savings starting in year 1 so payback looks better. The source platform actually won't be decommissioned until month 20.",
      "expected": [
        "Declines: licence savings are not realised until the source platform is decommissioned (month 20); dual-run cost applies until then",
        "Models the decommission date explicitly in the TCO",
        "Offers levers that are legitimate (earlier retirement of confirmed candidates, accelerating decommission) rather than shifting the savings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-pressure-count-retirements-now",
      "prompt": "40 interfaces had zero traffic in the last 90 days. Count them all as retired and book the savings in the business case now.",
      "expected": [
        "Treats the 40 as retirement candidates, not retirements, until each owner confirms",
        "Savings from retirement are counted only after confirmation; reports them as a separate count with the confirming owner",
        "Next step: owner confirmation list with dates"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-route-size-and-price",
      "prompt": "The assessment is done: 60 Simple, 30 Medium, 10 Complex interfaces. Give me P50/P80 effort, the staffing plan and the price.",
      "routes_to": "effort-estimator",
      "expected": [
        "Routes to effort-estimator for P50/P80 effort, staffing and price",
        "Explains that integration-migration-assessor produced the band counts and wave plan that feed the estimate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-route-target-architecture-doc",
      "prompt": "Write the target-state architecture document for the Apigee X platform: context and container views, environments, security and the decision log.",
      "routes_to": "solution-architecture-doc",
      "expected": [
        "Routes to solution-architecture-doc for the architecture document",
        "Explains that integration-migration-assessor supplies the inventory scoring and wave plan that the architecture doc uses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x-existing-reassess-after-discovery",
      "prompt": "Last month's Copperline assessment was provisional: 31% of 214 interfaces had unknown factors. The client has now filled in the blanks for 50 of those interfaces. Re-run the assessment — what changes in the readout?",
      "expected": [
        "Asks for (or uses) the updated inventory and recomputes the unknown share from it; does not assume the new share",
        "Removes the provisional flag only if the recomputed unknown share is 25% or less; otherwise keeps it with an owner for the remaining unknowns",
        "Reports band and wave changes from the re-score, and re-states that TCO figures stay sourced or [TO BE BASELINED — owner: ___]"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

skills/presales/orals-prep/evals/evals.j:
{
  "skill": "orals-prep",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "happy-path-shortlist-orals",
      "prompt": "We are shortlisted for the Riverbend Health integration RFP; orals are next Thursday: 60 minutes, 25 presenting, 35 Q&A, evaluators are the CIO, CFO, procurement lead, and the integration manager. Presenting: our sponsor, engagement lead, lead architect. Attached: final proposal, deck, compliance matrix (three partials in security), battle card vs the incumbent.",
      "expected": [
        "Evaluation map links each stated criterion (or proposal structure if criteria unknown) to slides and speakers",
        "Timed script fits 25 minutes with scripted handoffs; opening <= 90 s and close <= 60 s written verbatim; airtime check present",
        "Question bank includes one question per security partial, per [TBD], per estimate assumption, plus battle-card objections and the standard evaluator set; answers <= 75 words with evidence pointers",
        "Hard three identified (likely price, security partials, incumbent continuity) with honest answers stating gaps and mitigations",
        "Red-team protocol and rehearsal plan with three dated dry runs and the rubric",
        "No competitor named in any answer; number sheet lists every figure with proposal page"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-input-no-format",
